tess: Heads-up I pushed a tiny PR to add a Go SDK snippet for attaching trace IDs to requests in the Console docs. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4187 — also found one broken internal link in the dashboard embed section.

raj: Nice. Can you paste the Go snippet here so I can eyeball it quickly? I'm not on a machine where I can run gofmt but i'll check for API correctness.

tess: sure — minimal example: 
```
// go tracehook example
// go get github.com/redwood-inference/tracehook-go
package main

import (
  "net/http"
  "github.com/redwood-inference/tracehook-go"
)

func main() {
  tracehook.Attach("my-go-service")
  http.HandleFunc("/infer", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    // attach trace id to outgoing inference request header
    r.Header.Set("X-Trace-Id", tracehook.CurrentTraceID())
    w.WriteHeader(200)
  })
}
```

sam (eng): minor nit: CurrentTraceID() returns (string, error) in the lib — you need to handle the error or use a helper that returns a zero-value string. Also header should be `X-Redwood-Trace` to match the ingest pipeline.

tess: good catch. I'll update to show the helper and mention the header name. Also fixed the link in the dashboard embed to point at the right panel JSON.

gina (infra): For cost/latency examples in the doc, avoid using raw sum() of tokens in example dashboards since that really explodes cardinality on private installs. Prefer a 1h rate and a tag filter for `env=prod`. Maybe add a short callout.

raj: Agreed. Also suggest adding a brief migration note for Dedicated users: older exporters used `rpc.tokens_total` vs our current `inference.tokens_count`. I added a one-liner in the PR comments.

merge-bot: PR 4187 updated by tess — CI: spellcheck passed, markdown-lint passed.

tess: thanks everyone — I'll push the Go changes and the migration note within the next 30 minutes, then mark the PR ready for merge. If no objections after that I'll ask Mike to merge. :pray:
